# Round sparkr3 (kind ab): the first ws+Spark decode number against ws alone, same binary, same lease. The Spark
# (GB10, driver 580.178.04) is the V4.1 expert tier node over the TCP wire (r1wire+r2compact+r3node landed in
# 1ace3447c, the kernel word adds of round r3b in this tree: the 580 driver has no atomic-reduction memop), bound by
# `BLOOMERY_TIER_NODES` under `--place bp`, the prompt fed as steps (a prompt batch refuses a node tier), one card
# budget of 48G on every card (the only spelling a node plan takes; 48G >= the A6000's usable 48.5 GB, so the stage
# keeps plan (a)'s share, and the node's tier is sized 48 GB on the shared Spark's ~80 GB free).
# [derived] sparktier report 4.3 rerun at wc = 150.7 us (rig-log 2026-11-04#sparkr0-wc): the node arm's step =
# front + max(wc, 142 us x (n - k), a + 80 us x k) a layer, a = the exposed tier round trip (card
# docs/cards/sparkr3-a.card predicts 110..175 us): at a = 110 +6.3..+9.6 %, a = 140 +5.2..+7.2 %, a = 170
# +2.8..+3.7 %, break-even a = 197..198; above it the arm is slower. The r3b kernel adds cost 2 launches a layer
# on the node (+2 c_node ~ +10 us of a). The node arm's tier holds ~2,400 experts the stage's host tier served in
# plan (a) (smoke 2026-11-05 04:04: host_slots 166 a layer with the node, 41 GB tier), the term the model prices.
# Effect = (node arm tok/s - plan (a) tok/s) / plan (a): the band below is the model at a in 110..175; a above
# break-even reads below the band (decide-below), never inside it.
kind: ab
question: does the ws with the Spark as its TCP expert tier node decode faster than the ws alone on the same prose
  prompt at depth 512, same binary, one lease?
term: tok/s @ n=96, prose P 512, A6000 stage, the node arm --place bp with the Spark tier over tcp, the plain arm
  --place a; both under BLOOMERY_CARD_BUDGET=48G and BLOOMERY_PREFILL=steps so the two loads differ only by the node
unit: %
predict: 2.8..9.6
rounds: 4
condition: one binary, every arm's load its own process; the Spark's tier_server loop up (cpuidle-shallow started),
  its caches dropped before the sitting, free >= 60 GB; the witness shows no [cpu-busy] on a counted row (a compile
  on the box spoils it); rows marked [cold] stand with that mark
decide-in: the first ws+Spark decode number: write it with its interval at four rounds, then the a profile
  (sparkr3-a) and the code corpus at >= 6 rounds
decide-below: below -2: a is above break-even on this link; take the a profile before any lever (the pump hop, the
  node's H2D, the ack)
decide-above: above 10: the host tier's share moved more than the model's n - k term; read host_slots of both arms
